From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:54:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] split-only patch: rebase onto FlyTheElephant1 master a5f28aa
 (SOV-022)

The patch's base, test/console-collapse-pr14-pr17 at 121edd0, was
force-pushed away upstream and can no longer be fetched, so nobody could
build the split-only C gateway from the published instructions. Rebased onto
master a5f28aa, which reworked what the patch touches: one coinbase class for
every BLAKE2b miner, a subsidy-only coinbase for new blocks, the DRS resume
extension in the hello, and anti-withholding.

- Split-only is one check in send_mining_notify after
  datum_stratum_coinbase_index: while pooled, no notify for type 0, the
  subsidy-only coinbase, or a job whose coinbaser produced no split.
- "nta-v1\0" follows the DRS resume extension, where Prime reads it for this
  lineage.
- Master mines BLAKE2b only: every LZT1 variant is attested, and the SHA256d
  case and its test are gone.
- The LZT1 unit test configures a pool without anti-withholding and restores
  the default afterwards.

Builds; ./datum_gateway --test passes on a5f28aa.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
